    "chainBSilenceWaitNote": "The candidate chain's own end-of-turn policy knob, fixed here before the run: after the shipping VAD (endpointMs=400) declares speech_stopped, wait an ADDITIONAL 700 ms; if speech resumes inside that window the utterance was a hesitation and continues. So the chain's effective end-of-turn silence is 400+700=1100 ms. 700 ms is chosen to sit above a natural intra-clause pause (~100-400 ms in the synthesiser's prosody) and below a deliberate thought pause (>1 s). It is a declared design constant, NOT tuned to any sample's outcome: the pause samples (s2/s3) were authored with injected pauses ABOVE this window precisely to test whether the chain degrades honestly when a hesitation crosses the wait.",
